WEBVTT

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:22.122
Though you are so close,
Kore hodo soba ni

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:26.626
I cannot tell you how I feel.
Iru no ni tsutaerarezu

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:30.697
The more strongly I feel,
Tsuyoku omou hodo

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:35.301
the harder it is for me to find the words.
Kotoba ga mitsukaranai

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:43.343
What is sad is not fate...
Kanashii no wa unmei ja nakute

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:54.117
...but that all encounters come to an end.
Deai no subete ni owari ga aru koto

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:58.558
O incomplete beings,
Mikan naru mono

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.996
awaken, for beyond the night...
mezameyo yoru o koetara

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:07.067
At the end of the desert...
Sabaku no hate ni

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:14.735
...the truth surely awaits you.
Shinjitsu ga matteru yo kitto

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:38.528
There is a sad tale from a time gone by.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.392
This soul was born in the company of sorrow.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:47.165
People fought over him.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.140
A war with no victory or defeat.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:56.511
It was a kind of madness.

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:19.032
He fell into a long slumber.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.738
What is that?

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:28.369
Let's turn back.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:32.118
Confirming that such a thing exists here...

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.814
...should be enough to fulfill
your current job, should it not?

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.214
Miss Honoka?

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.291
I can't.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:38.655
What?

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.081
Something's calling.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.852
Something's calling to me from inside there.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:44.821
I have to go.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:49.800
Battling Against Illusion

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:56.607
You'd better not have intentionally
overlooked his approach.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.836
What do you mean by that?

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.270
If you wished for his intervention...

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.084
If you thought he would actively
take part in this situation,

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.574
that was clearly mistaken of you.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.381
He will do nothing.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:11.284
He is not our enemy, but nor is he our ally.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.415
I am aware of that.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:18.459
In fact, I do not think he should
intervene in this planet's affairs.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.055
That is what I believe.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:24.402
Though, that is not to say that
I am entirely without hope.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:29.842
Rather, it is her that I am concerned about.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:30.900
Honoka?

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:35.247
Since that incident occurred,
I have investigated her.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.548
Just who she is.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:42.982
And why you are so fascinated with her.

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:44.821
What did you find out?

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.457
Nothing much.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:47.954
But it worries me.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:51.998
Perhaps that young lady
has something within her...

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:56.458
...that is even greater
than what you or I imagine.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:04:00.565
However, that may just be a
faint hope of mine as well.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:05.473
As planned, the wormhole driver
will attack the target in 6 hours.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.179
I will see you again later.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:21.092
Hey, isn't it kind of growing bigger?

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:24.396
The speed at which the dome is
swelling has increased from earlier.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.122
It will be dangerous to stay here.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:27.358
Hono!

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.498
Let's go back.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.838
What's calling you anyway?!

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.640
I don't know. But...

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.699
You can't go into something that strange!

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.370
It'd be better not to get
involved in this any further!

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:40.578
Hono!

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.081
Hey!

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.745
You stop her, too!

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:47.508
Damn.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:48.382
Hono?!

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.220
Hold on!

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:51.624
Come on!

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:53.654
Hey, Hono!

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.773
What in the world was that?

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.056
Huh?

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:23.988
What is this?

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:31.527
Those are...

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.503
Wh-What's going on here?!

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.994
Why am I getting attacked?!

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.604
And where am I anyway?!

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:49.248
Give me a break! What's going on?!

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.442
Why is this suddenly...

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:55.984
Hono...

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:57.152
Hono, where are you?!

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.258
Hono?! Hono!

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.022
Hono, are you not here?! Answer me!

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:05.765
Bogie!

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:06.254
You okay?

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:08.935
Am I okay?! Where the heck are we?

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:09.867
The desert.

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:10.859
What are you sayin-

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.628
The radar shows everything is normal.

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:15.074
Though, it seems to differ
with what's on the monitor.

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:18.009
What kind of nonsense is that?!
You must be an idiot!

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:19.100
I am functioning normally.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.181
Return fire!

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:24.183
It's no use. I can't lock on to them.

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.585
I don't care! Just fire!

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:27.353
I am saying that I cannot hit them.

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.589
The trajectories should be intersecting,

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:30.957
but there's absolutely no reaction.

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:32.291
Striking them is impossible.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:33.883
Then look for Hono!

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.728
I don't need you to tell me that.
I'm already doing it.

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:36.829
We don't need to worry about Iks?

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.558
If you want to look for him, go ahead.

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:43.000
Hono!

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:40.915
What is this?

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:47.761
Honoka!

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:50.558
Hono!

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.538
Hono!

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:57.876
Don't touch her!

00:07:58.444 --> 00:07:58.933
Hono?!

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.009
Guess the secret's out...

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:10.787
Bogie, hurry!

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:23.236
You struck it, didn't you?

00:08:23.236 --> 00:08:24.669
I struck it, but...

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:26.232
I was able to strike it,

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:28.231
but it wasn't real.

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:31.573
Let's go back.

00:08:31.811 --> 00:08:34.013
The sensors aren't functioning at all.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:37.316
I'm having difficulty even determining
our current location.

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:38.840
You just have to back up!

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:40.753
We cannot escape from here.

00:08:40.753 --> 00:08:41.651
What?

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:44.255
We are not in an ordinary space here.

00:08:44.557 --> 00:08:46.889
Even if we were to drive until our fuel ran out,

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:49.325
we would probably only end up
right where we started.

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:50.521
What do you mean?

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:52.790
Hey, you!

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:54.791
Tell us, Iks.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:58.265
How are you feeling?

00:08:58.504 --> 00:09:00.840
It looks like your healing's been effective.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.501
I feel a little better.

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:05.406
More importantly, you know, don't you?

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:08.969
What is this place?
What was all that chaos we just saw?

00:09:11.017 --> 00:09:14.714
I know you can't talk to us about stuff like that.

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:16.182
But...

00:09:21.694 --> 00:09:24.720
There is a sad tale...

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:27.199
Wormhole, stable.

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:30.726
The countdown is progressing smoothly.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:36.799
Gravestone may be trying to cross
into our world from the other side.

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:39.700
The distortion may be a result of that,

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:42.312
a sort of threshold between the two spaces.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:45.711
But even so, why now?

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:47.345
Gravestone?

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:49.314
Then what about what we saw earlier?

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:51.083
Probably his memories.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:54.015
He took the memory of the attack
launched against him...

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.287
...and unleashed it against us.

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:59.465
It appears that in this space,

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:02.068
the psyche itself operates as a direct force.

00:10:02.068 --> 00:10:04.468
What? So it's a psychic attack?

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:07.036
One powerful enough to affect even Bogie?

00:10:07.707 --> 00:10:11.010
If Miss Honoka had not unleashed
her chi and struck that battlefield,

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:14.207
we may have been killed by the illusion.

00:10:14.747 --> 00:10:16.578
Psyche against psyche, huh?

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:21.047
Then, that means this weapon
is hostile towards us?

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:23.055
Unfortunately.

00:10:23.055 --> 00:10:25.157
This is unbelievable. Why?

00:10:25.157 --> 00:10:27.819
Why is a weapon from the
Great War becoming active now?

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:29.053
That is...

00:10:30.997 --> 00:10:31.793
I have to go.

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:33.466
Miss Honoka!

00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:34.694
Hey, Hono!

00:10:36.035 --> 00:10:39.138
Hold on! Where do you think
you're going in your condition?!

00:10:39.138 --> 00:10:40.973
You can tell, can't you, Teacher?

00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:41.302
What?

00:10:41.741 --> 00:10:43.409
There's chi flowing...

00:10:43.409 --> 00:10:45.309
It's all converging at one point somewhere.

00:10:46.746 --> 00:10:47.838
I have to go.

00:10:48.114 --> 00:10:49.248
He's calling me.

00:10:49.248 --> 00:10:50.383
Who is?

00:10:50.383 --> 00:10:52.317
This weapon thing, whatever it's called?

00:10:52.618 --> 00:10:53.919
I don't know.

00:10:53.919 --> 00:10:56.288
But if there's no one else here, then probably.

00:10:56.288 --> 00:10:57.482
Don't say such ridiculous things!

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.694
Even assuming that it's really here,
why would it call to you?

00:11:01.694 --> 00:11:02.294
That's just...

00:11:02.294 --> 00:11:03.488
Please, Teacher.

00:11:08.467 --> 00:11:09.695
Sit tight.

00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:12.732
We'll try to collect more information.

00:11:13.239 --> 00:11:14.073
But...

00:11:14.073 --> 00:11:15.472
Be quiet and do as I say!

00:11:21.447 --> 00:11:22.277
Come on.

00:11:30.156 --> 00:11:32.590
Iks, let's go talk over there.

00:11:32.658 --> 00:11:33.625
All right.

00:11:38.497 --> 00:11:40.397
You behave yourself now.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.635
The way you are right now,
even I could beat you.

00:12:03.522 --> 00:12:06.286
Wormhole driver firing in T-minus two hours.

00:12:06.959 --> 00:12:08.984
It looks like it will work.

00:12:09.462 --> 00:12:10.486
So it seems.

00:12:13.099 --> 00:12:14.123
Is something the matter?

00:12:15.701 --> 00:12:17.236
We suffered losses in the war...

00:12:17.236 --> 00:12:20.865
...and we lose again because of
a negative legacy left by the war.

00:12:21.907 --> 00:12:24.977
In order to clear away a nightmare
that wasn't supposed to exist,

00:12:24.977 --> 00:12:27.639
we awaken a nightmare
that didn't exist before.

00:12:28.214 --> 00:12:30.045
At times, I wonder...

00:12:30.316 --> 00:12:33.683
...that perhaps we are
caught in a misguided cycle.

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:38.824
That as long as we are caught within it,
nothing will change,

00:12:38.824 --> 00:12:41.088
no matter how much effort we expend.

00:12:41.293 --> 00:12:43.362
If such a cycle were to exist,

00:12:43.362 --> 00:12:45.455
we have but to break it with our own hands.

00:12:45.664 --> 00:12:46.858
Am I wrong?

00:12:50.603 --> 00:12:51.934
That is true.

00:12:53.639 --> 00:12:55.072
Bogie, what's the situation?

00:12:55.574 --> 00:12:56.768
No changes.

00:12:56.842 --> 00:12:58.744
The sensors show no response whatsoever.

00:12:58.744 --> 00:12:59.574
I see.

00:13:00.246 --> 00:13:04.808
As I said before, we are not in a normal space.

00:13:05.618 --> 00:13:07.186
The means to escape it are...

00:13:07.186 --> 00:13:08.949
Then what do you plan to do?!

00:13:09.155 --> 00:13:11.924
You're awfully knowledgeable about
the Great War and this space,

00:13:11.924 --> 00:13:13.526
and you've got those healing powers...

00:13:13.526 --> 00:13:15.016
Just who are you?

00:13:17.696 --> 00:13:19.254
You do something about it!

00:13:19.532 --> 00:13:21.557
Since you seem to be the most
knowledgeable about this place.

00:13:22.034 --> 00:13:23.296
I am sorry.

00:13:28.641 --> 00:13:30.233
Is there something on your mind?

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:32.301
That girl...

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:34.803
Is Hono one of The Third?

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:38.810
That is not for me to say.

00:13:39.385 --> 00:13:41.114
Please ask her yourself.

00:13:41.587 --> 00:13:45.224
She seems to like you,
so I'm sure she'll tell you.

00:13:45.224 --> 00:13:46.992
Don't give me that crap.

00:13:46.992 --> 00:13:48.687
I can tell, just by watching.

00:13:49.361 --> 00:13:51.921
Since I joined up, I have heard a lot about you.

00:13:52.865 --> 00:13:54.526
She was annoyed, wasn't she?

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:56.430
Yes, it was a hailstorm of criticisms.

00:13:57.436 --> 00:13:59.238
You do not listen to her.

00:13:59.238 --> 00:14:00.272
You are not a morning person,

00:14:00.272 --> 00:14:03.309
but you complain if she
has breakfast without you.

00:14:03.309 --> 00:14:05.641
You walk around naked inside the tank.

00:14:06.145 --> 00:14:08.306
You cannot organize your belongings at all.

00:14:08.848 --> 00:14:10.616
She has never seen someone like you.

00:14:10.616 --> 00:14:12.311
No one she has met is worse.

00:14:13.085 --> 00:14:14.720
She told me so most cheerfully.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:15.186
What?

00:14:21.527 --> 00:14:25.691
She never went to school,
because she grew up in a caravan.

00:14:26.065 --> 00:14:29.034
So she has apparently wanted to
experience calling someone "Teacher".

00:14:30.803 --> 00:14:31.792
Stupid girl.

00:15:00.499 --> 00:15:02.967
Paife, Iks, take a look in the cabin.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:05.898
What? What is it?

00:15:07.239 --> 00:15:08.035
Hono...

00:15:08.107 --> 00:15:10.439
I checked, but she's not on board.

00:15:13.078 --> 00:15:14.739
Hono?! Hono?!

00:15:18.384 --> 00:15:20.477
What's going on?! Did she get off?!

00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:22.388
You were watching her, weren't you?!

00:15:22.388 --> 00:15:25.152
The internal monitors and sensors
were continually operating.

00:15:25.658 --> 00:15:28.894
Then what?! Are you going to tell me
she was gone before you knew it?!

00:15:28.894 --> 00:15:30.657
I can think of no other way to put it.

00:15:32.097 --> 00:15:32.529
Iks!

00:15:35.901 --> 00:15:37.596
Bogie, where's Iks?

00:15:37.903 --> 00:15:38.995
I don't know.

00:15:39.104 --> 00:15:40.867
He's nowhere to be found on board.

00:15:41.774 --> 00:15:42.365
He's disappeared.

00:15:45.544 --> 00:15:46.704
It can't be...

00:15:54.386 --> 00:15:56.445
How had she gotten off the tank?

00:15:56.855 --> 00:15:58.880
She had absolutely no recollection.

00:15:59.858 --> 00:16:04.124
It merely felt like her senses
had shifted for a moment.

00:16:05.431 --> 00:16:08.628
Thinking back, she had been feeling
something since before the job.

00:16:09.368 --> 00:16:13.805
It may be that she had not
taken the job for the pay.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:17.343
It seemed as if she had been
called by this voice from the start...

00:16:17.343 --> 00:16:20.403
...and she had headed out here in
order to find out who was calling her.

00:16:21.413 --> 00:16:23.244
That was the feeling she got.

00:16:35.327 --> 00:16:37.158
Bogie, stay on this course.

00:16:37.262 --> 00:16:38.320
Fixing course.

00:16:38.931 --> 00:16:41.700
Moving around haphazardly is very risky.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:43.167
We could also wait.

00:16:43.402 --> 00:16:45.029
I can read chi, too.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.373
I think I can figure out where that girl's gone.

00:16:47.373 --> 00:16:47.973
But...

00:16:47.973 --> 00:16:48.439
Just do it!

00:16:52.378 --> 00:16:54.209
I saw that girl in town.

00:16:55.247 --> 00:16:56.976
I'd never seen a girl like that.

00:16:57.449 --> 00:17:00.077
It's a lie that I came here at Ingrid's request.

00:17:00.719 --> 00:17:02.880
The truth is, I asked to come.

00:17:03.455 --> 00:17:06.091
When I heard that woman had hired Hono.

00:17:06.091 --> 00:17:07.319
I had no idea.

00:17:07.726 --> 00:17:10.286
You see, I get attached to people really easily.

00:17:10.596 --> 00:17:12.731
But I get disinterested quickly, too,

00:17:12.731 --> 00:17:15.601
and the moment I think the person
isn't what I expected them to be,

00:17:15.601 --> 00:17:16.898
it's bye-bye.

00:17:17.136 --> 00:17:20.305
I get attached on my own,
get disappointed on my own,

00:17:20.305 --> 00:17:21.738
and say goodbye on my own.

00:17:22.741 --> 00:17:24.606
That's why I don't have friends.

00:17:26.378 --> 00:17:29.014
I wanted to see for myself,

00:17:29.014 --> 00:17:33.383
that she was someone worthy of my interest.

00:17:34.086 --> 00:17:36.247
Your question has been satisfied, has it not?

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:42.686
That girl said that was the first
time she'd killed a person, right?

00:17:43.929 --> 00:17:45.191
It's so stupid.

00:17:45.297 --> 00:17:47.356
Being shaken up by something like that.

00:17:47.699 --> 00:17:51.499
If she hadn't killed that man,
I would've been killed.

00:17:51.637 --> 00:17:53.229
There was no other choice!

00:17:53.338 --> 00:17:54.999
She must have been able to do it before!

00:17:55.374 --> 00:17:57.842
She could've just had faith in
the judgment call she made!

00:17:58.310 --> 00:17:59.445
It's really so stupid!

00:17:59.445 --> 00:18:02.107
Otherwise, it just makes me wretched
for having been saved!

00:18:02.281 --> 00:18:04.112
It's just unbelievable to me.

00:18:05.284 --> 00:18:06.273
I understand.

00:18:06.452 --> 00:18:08.852
You must really like Miss Honoka.

00:18:09.121 --> 00:18:10.053
What?

00:18:18.831 --> 00:18:20.321
Life sign reading straight ahead.

00:18:21.467 --> 00:18:22.263
Hono?

00:18:23.602 --> 00:18:24.591
No...

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.029
Who is it?

00:18:45.891 --> 00:18:46.949
Who are you?

00:18:47.593 --> 00:18:49.754
I am the one who awoke you.

00:18:49.995 --> 00:18:51.087
Awoke me?

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:54.063
I see, so that was you.

00:18:54.333 --> 00:18:57.063
You brushed past this place
where I reside and flew on.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:01.237
It seems I startled you. I apologize.

00:19:02.007 --> 00:19:03.975
I knew about you.

00:19:04.243 --> 00:19:07.212
It was just poorly anticipated on my part...

00:19:07.212 --> 00:19:09.009
...that it would impact you in this way.

00:19:09.615 --> 00:19:12.049
I thought you'd come to kill me.

00:19:12.518 --> 00:19:14.952
That you'd finally come in, even here.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.523
Even though that should
have been impossible.

00:19:17.523 --> 00:19:19.718
At the very least,
I have no animosity towards you.

00:19:20.125 --> 00:19:23.595
The fact I awoke you was a mere coincidence.

00:19:23.595 --> 00:19:26.962
I see. So that really was the case.

00:19:27.733 --> 00:19:30.369
No one pays any attention to me.

00:19:30.369 --> 00:19:33.138
Rather, they tried to kill me!

00:19:33.138 --> 00:19:35.240
I wasn't able to do anything.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.242
Taking refuge here was all I could do.

00:19:37.242 --> 00:19:40.846
But you are now trying to
come out from this place.

00:19:40.846 --> 00:19:41.980
Why is that?

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:43.277
That's obvious.

00:19:43.482 --> 00:19:46.218
I'm going to do exactly what I ought to do.

00:19:46.218 --> 00:19:48.152
I have to get back at them.

00:19:48.453 --> 00:19:51.256
And I'll wipe out everything there is.

00:19:51.256 --> 00:19:53.281
The world that hated me.

00:19:53.425 --> 00:19:55.985
That world that tried to wipe me out!

00:20:05.704 --> 00:20:06.966
Where are you going?

00:20:07.272 --> 00:20:08.500
I don't know.

00:20:08.774 --> 00:20:10.332
I'm looking for someone.

00:20:10.509 --> 00:20:11.510
Who?

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:12.744
A girl.

00:20:12.744 --> 00:20:13.506
I know where she is.

00:20:14.079 --> 00:20:16.604
Then tell me. Where did she go?

00:20:16.982 --> 00:20:19.712
I can't tell you and telling you
would be pointless anyway.

00:20:20.085 --> 00:20:20.710
Why?

00:20:21.153 --> 00:20:23.713
Because you will die here.

00:20:24.389 --> 00:20:27.688
Wormhole driver firing in T-minus one hour.

00:21:43.669 --> 00:21:44.499
You're here.

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:48.006
A flexible civilization...
Juunan na bunmei wa

00:21:48.006 --> 00:21:50.509
...is always rapidly advancing.
Itsudatte nisshin-geppo

00:21:50.509 --> 00:21:53.478
You and your dreams are also...
Kimi to yume mo

00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:57.278
...making headway even now.
Genzai shinkou

00:22:02.788 --> 00:22:05.757
I realized for the first time...
Hajimete kizuitan da

00:22:05.757 --> 00:22:09.454
...with that line, resembling a surprise attack.
Fui-uchi ni nita sono serifu de

00:22:14.499 --> 00:22:17.436
My sixth sense was pried open.
Kojiakerareta dai-rokkan

00:22:17.436 --> 00:22:21.463
I'd been waiting for this feeling this whole time.
Kono kankaku o zutto matteita

00:22:25.477 --> 00:22:28.447
Opening my heart, just opening it...
Kokoro o hiraite tada hiraite

00:22:28.447 --> 00:22:31.416
I embrace the voices of strangers.
Daisansha no koe ukeireru

00:22:31.416 --> 00:22:34.286
Earnestly persevering, just persevering...
Hitasura koraete tada koraete

00:22:34.286 --> 00:22:37.380
I even try turning pages of criticism.
Hinan no peeji mo aketemiru

00:22:37.689 --> 00:22:40.659
I'm going to leave my...
Toushindai no boku wa

00:22:40.659 --> 00:22:43.595
...true-to-life self behind, right here.
Koko ni oite iku yo

00:22:43.595 --> 00:22:47.432
You can say whatever you want now...
Mou nanto itte kuretemo

00:22:47.432 --> 00:22:48.956
...and I'm fine with that.
Kekkou da

00:22:49.468 --> 00:22:54.940
Ah, how simple is the impulse to evolve.
Aa nante tanjun da shinka shitai to iu shoudou

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:57.843
You and your dreams are also...
Kimi to yume mo

00:22:57.843 --> 00:23:01.040
...making headway even now.
Genzai shinkou

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.889
Preview

00:23:17.129 --> 00:23:19.290
The wormhole driver's countdown...

00:23:19.698 --> 00:23:21.962
Her imminent death proclaimed to Teacher...

00:23:22.367 --> 00:23:24.562
When everything was approaching the end,

00:23:24.636 --> 00:23:26.831
before me was me.

00:23:27.339 --> 00:23:30.075
She drew her own sword
and came swinging at me,

00:23:30.075 --> 00:23:32.771
but I was unable to draw my sword.

00:23:33.011 --> 00:23:36.674
And then, a blade pierced my chest...

00:23:37.449 --> 00:23:40.752
Next time on
The Third - The Girl With The Blue Eye,

00:23:40.752 --> 00:23:42.053
episode 12, "Their Respective Reasons".

00:23:42.053 --> 00:23:43.321
Their Respective Reasons
episode 12, "Their Respective Reasons".

00:23:43.321 --> 00:23:44.913
Their Respective Reasons
